# Task Manager

Task Manager is a Windows utility used to monitor and manage the system.

It provides information about:

- Running Applications
- Background Processes
- CPU Usage
- Memory Usage
- Disk Usage
- Network Usage
- GPU Usage
- Startup Applications
- Logged-in Users
- Windows Services

Shortcut:

```text
Ctrl + Shift + Esc
```

---

# Processes Tab

The Processes tab displays:

- Running applications
- Background processes
- Windows processes

It is commonly used to identify applications consuming excessive CPU or Memory resources.

Examples:

- Microsoft Edge
- File Explorer
- Microsoft Teams
- Google Chrome

---

# Performance Tab

The Performance tab provides real-time monitoring of:

- CPU Utilization
- Memory Usage
- Disk Activity
- Ethernet/Wi-Fi Usage
- GPU Usage

This helps IT Support technicians identify system performance bottlenecks.

---

# Startup Apps Tab

The Startup Apps tab displays programs that automatically launch when Windows starts.

Examples:

- Microsoft Teams
- OneDrive
- Spotify
- Discord

Too many enabled startup applications can increase Windows boot time and reduce overall system performance.

---

# Users Tab

Displays:

- Logged-in users
- Resource usage for each user
- Session status

Useful in environments where multiple users share a computer.

---

# Services Tab

Displays Windows services and their current status.

Status examples:

- Running
- Stopped

Examples:

- Windows Update
- Print Spooler
- Windows Defender Services

